event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":84,"item_id":"rs_001b2381cb11a4b8016aca832be44881978ac681d2513dcc88","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Evaluating shared date validator implementation**\n\nI’m considering if I have enough time to implement a shared date validator module. The simplest approach might be to duplicate the pure browser validator without changing the server stack. I think testing the adapter beforehand is crucial, especially since the input gets detached after rendering. I should rename and assert the old input to ensure everything works fine. Plus, adding broad tests seems like a good idea to cover more scenarios."}

